# Cloudflare Pages - HTTP headers
# https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/headers/

# HSTS is a COMMITMENT, not a toggle: once a browser has seen this header it
# refuses plain HTTP for this domain until max-age expires, and there is no way
# to reach those users and tell them otherwise.
#
# Deliberately conservative to start:
#   max-age=86400      one day, so a mistake ages out by tomorrow
#   no includeSubDomains  would cover every future subdomain, incl. any staging host
#   no preload         submits the domain to a list baked into browser binaries;
#                      removal takes months. Do not add it casually.
# Once this has run clean for a few days, raise max-age to 15552000 (6 months).
#
# NOTE: this is only half the job. http://saadm.dev/ still answers 200 because
# "Always Use HTTPS" is a Cloudflare zone setting, not a header - HSTS only binds
# a browser that has already reached the site over HTTPS once. Turn that on in
# SSL/TLS -> Edge Certificates, and add a www -> apex 301 redirect rule.
/*
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=86400
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), microphone=(), camera=()
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://unpkg.com https://cdn.jsdelivr.net https://static.cloudflareinsights.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://fonts.googleapis.com https://unpkg.com; font-src 'self' https://fonts.gstatic.com; img-src 'self' data: blob: https://images.unsplash.com https://*.tile.openstreetmap.org https://*.basemaps.cartocdn.com https://unpkg.com; connect-src 'self' https://formsubmit.co https://huggingface.co https://*.hf.co https://cdn.jsdelivr.net https://cloudflareinsights.com https://static.cloudflareinsights.com; worker-src 'self' blob:; child-src 'self' blob:; frame-ancestors 'self'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self' https://formsubmit.co; object-src 'none'

# Short cache + revalidate for project JS/CSS - these files don't have fingerprints in
# their names so they need to revalidate often. (Was: max-age=31536000 immutable -
# which locked stale code in browser caches for up to a year. Don't do that.)
/app/css/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=300, must-revalidate
/app/js/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=300, must-revalidate
/app/api/qc/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
